<hr data-start=3D"457" data-end=3D"460">
<h1 data-start=3D"462" data-end=3D"499">=F0=9F=93=98 Tutoriel SQL : <code d=
ata-start=3D"482" data-end=3D"499">FULL OUTER JOIN</code></h1>
<hr data-start=3D"501" data-end=3D"504">
<h2 data-start=3D"506" data-end=3D"534">=F0=9F=8E=AF Objectifs p=C3=A9dagog=
iques</h2>
<p data-start=3D"536" data-end=3D"574">=C3=80 la fin de ce chapitre, vous s=
aurez :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"576" data-end=3D"875">
<li data-start=3D"576" data-end=3D"623">
<p data-start=3D"578" data-end=3D"623">Comprendre le principe d=E2=80=99un =
<code data-start=3D"606" data-end=3D"623">FULL OUTER JOIN</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"624" data-end=3D"688">
<p data-start=3D"626" data-end=3D"688">Diff=C3=A9rencier les types de joint=
ures (INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"689" data-end=3D"760">
<p data-start=3D"691" data-end=3D"760">Utiliser <code data-start=3D"700" da=
ta-end=3D"717">FULL OUTER JOIN</code> dans des sc=C3=A9narios de donn=C3=A9=
es asym=C3=A9triques</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"761" data-end=3D"818">
<p data-start=3D"763" data-end=3D"818">G=C3=A9rer les valeurs <code data-st=
art=3D"781" data-end=3D"787">NULL</code> issues de la jointure compl=C3=A8t=
e</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"819" data-end=3D"875">
<p data-start=3D"821" data-end=3D"875">Appliquer <code data-start=3D"831" d=
ata-end=3D"848">FULL OUTER JOIN</code> =C3=A0 des cas m=C3=A9tiers concrets=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"877" data-end=3D"880">
<h2 data-start=3D"882" data-end=3D"923">=F0=9F=94=B0 1. Introduction =C3=A0=
 <code data-start=3D"906" data-end=3D"923">FULL OUTER JOIN</code></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"925" data-end=3D"942">=F0=9F=94=8E D=C3=A9finition</h3>
<p data-start=3D"944" data-end=3D"1021">Une <strong data-start=3D"948" data=
-end=3D"977">jointure externe compl=C3=A8te</strong> (<code data-start=3D"9=
79" data-end=3D"996">FULL OUTER JOIN</code>) combine les effets de :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1023" data-end=3D"1135">
<li data-start=3D"1023" data-end=3D"1078">
<p data-start=3D"1025" data-end=3D"1078"><code data-start=3D"1025" data-end=
=3D"1036">LEFT JOIN</code> (toutes les lignes de la table de gauche)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1079" data-end=3D"1135">
<p data-start=3D"1081" data-end=3D"1135"><code data-start=3D"1081" data-end=
=3D"1093">RIGHT JOIN</code> (toutes les lignes de la table de droite)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1137" data-end=3D"1219">=F0=9F=93=8C Elle <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"1145" data-end=3D"1189">inclut toutes les lignes des deux tables</str=
ong>, avec ou sans correspondance.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1221" data-end=3D"1303">Les colonnes issues de la table sa=
ns correspondance sont remplies avec <strong data-start=3D"1292" data-end=
=3D"1302"><code data-start=3D"1294" data-end=3D"1300">NULL</code></strong>.=
</p>
