<hr data-start=3D"3408" data-end=3D"3411">
<h2 data-start=3D"3413" data-end=3D"3463">=F0=9F=A7=A0 5. Mode autocommit (=
=C3=A0 comprendre absolument)</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3465" data-end=3D"3555">Dans de nombreux SGBD, chaque requ=
=C3=AAte est <strong data-start=3D"3507" data-end=3D"3534">automatiquement =
engag=C3=A9e</strong> (<code data-start=3D"3536" data-end=3D"3553">autocomm=
it =3D ON</code>).</p>
<p data-start=3D"3557" data-end=3D"3572">Cela signifie :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3574" data-end=3D"3719">
<li data-start=3D"3574" data-end=3D"3639">
<p data-start=3D"3576" data-end=3D"3639">Chaque <code data-start=3D"3583" d=
ata-end=3D"3591">INSERT</code>, <code data-start=3D"3593" data-end=3D"3601"=
>UPDATE</code>, <code data-start=3D"3603" data-end=3D"3611">DELETE</code> e=
st imm=C3=A9diatement <code data-start=3D"3630" data-end=3D"3638">COMMIT</c=
ode>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3640" data-end=3D"3719">
<p data-start=3D"3642" data-end=3D"3719">Il faut <strong data-start=3D"3650=
" data-end=3D"3677">d=C3=A9sactiver l'autocommit</strong> pour g=C3=A9rer m=
anuellement les transactions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
